+# Pass 4 (same day) — the T2 hash oracle is BUILT and PROVEN (tier 1 of the two-tier gate)
+
+**Verdict.** [`arms/gate-server-arms.sh`](arms/gate-server-arms.sh) is the gate T2 will be measured against, and it
+already answers the question that shapes the next session: **the reference the two-arm server has to reproduce is
+stable, and the gate fires when the numbers move.**  Three server runs, one at a time (`HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0`),
+product shape (arena 5000, `-ncmoe 40 -lme auto`, `-c 8192 -ub 512 -np 2`), both purity pins, two concurrent
+requests (two ~500-token slices of `prompts/kld-corpus-35b-in-domain.txt`, `n_predict 32`, `temp 0`, `seed 42`):
+
+| run | SLOT 0 | SLOT 1 | tier-2 census | tier 1 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `ref-run1` | **`459865c93d55cbaf`** | **`7dc20b0ce0bac255`** | `h=0.6853` (42151/61504) | — |
+| `ref-run2` (a second server process) | `459865c93d55cbaf` | `7dc20b0ce0bac255` | `h=0.6853` | **PASS** (identical) |
+| `ref-ub256` (`-ub 256`: a real shape/numerics change) | `182a9fcfe1de6a70` | `7dc20b0ce0bac255` | `h=0.6323` | **FAIL** (as it must) |
+| `ref-npad` (`LLAMA_KV_N_PAD_MIN=8192`) | `459865c93d55cbaf` | `7dc20b0ce0bac255` | `h=0.6820` | PASS, census differs |
+
+So: the reference text is **deterministic across separate server processes** (2/2, both slots, same census), and the
+gate **detects a numerics change** (`-ub 256` moves slot 0's reply and its census).  Two things that are worth
+knowing before T2 is written:
+
+* **`LLAMA_KV_N_PAD_MIN` does not move this server's text** (it moves only the tier-2 census) — unlike the
+  instrument's warm 2-slot scenario in pass 1.  So it is a *tier-2* sensitivity control, never the text control.
+  `-ub` is the text control.
+* **The compare is defined on the text only** (`SLOT` lines), with a vacuity guard: a result file with no `SLOT`
+  lines, or a slot that produced 0 tokens, is an ORACLE ERROR rather than a pass.  The census and handshake lines
+  are recorded so a difference has a mechanism attached; they are never asserted (tier 2 does that).
+
+**What the next session runs, first thing.**
+
+```bash
+cd wip/prefill-decode-arms/arms
+./gate-server-arms.sh --mode ref                 # -> runs/server-oracle/ref.txt
+./gate-server-arms.sh --mode arms                # needs --prefill-decode-arms in llama-server
+./gate-server-arms.sh --compare ../runs/server-oracle/ref.txt ../runs/server-oracle/arms.txt
+```
+
+The reference hashes above are the acceptance values (they are also in `runs/server-oracle/ref-run1.txt`); the arm
+run must read **both** slots identically and print `HANDSHAKE the pair shares one allocation owner`.  If
+`--prefill-decode-arms` is not yet a flag, the server exits at start-up and the script says so — the gate cannot
+pass vacuously.
+
+Caveat: the census is **not** stable across rep counts/loads (`h=0.6853` here vs `0.6820`/`0.6323` for the controls),
+which is exactly why tier 2 exists and why tier 1 is the text.
+
+Files: [`arms/gate-server-arms.sh`](arms/gate-server-arms.sh), [`runs/server-oracle/`](runs/server-oracle/)
+(`ref-run1/2`, `ref-ub256`, `ref-npad` + the gzipped server logs).
